Chapter: GopZones
  cites Works chapter GopLocale

 The zone table: which places this machine can be, what each one is offset by,
 and which summer time rule it follows. It cites the calendar and nothing
 else, so a caller that wants to know what time it is somewhere does not drag
 a filesystem in with it.

 THIS IS NOT A TZDATA PORT AND MUST NOT GROW INTO ONE. It is a few dozen
 zones, hand written, carrying the rule each follows AS OF 2026-09-07. A
 government that moves a date makes one row here wrong, and the fix is a one
 line edit and a re-measure rather than a database. The design says this in
 the same words: `docs/Designs/Active/Apps/ClockAndZone.md`.

 The offsets are MINUTES because a sixth of the world does not live on a whole
 hour. India is +05:30, Nepal +05:45, Chatham +12:45, and a design that cannot
 say those cannot say where those people are.

Section: The Row

 `zr-stripe` is which of the 24 map bands the zone is drawn in, and it is the
 STANDARD offset rounded to an hour, never the summer one. A stripe that moved
 twice a year would make the map lie for half of it, and the map is the thing
 somebody uses to find their zone before they know its name.

  ZoneRow = record {
    zr-name : Text,
    zr-city : Text,
    zr-base : Integer,
    zr-rule : Integer,
    zr-stripe : Integer
  }

  zrow : Text, Text, Integer, Integer, Integer -> ZoneRow
  zrow (n) (c) (b) (r) (s) = ZoneRow { zr-name = n, zr-city = c, zr-base = b, zr-rule = r, zr-stripe = s }

Section: The Table

 Ordered west to east, because that is the order the map is in and the list
 sits beside the map. Within a stripe the ordering is by population, so the
 first row of a stripe is the one most people picking that stripe want.

  zone-rows : List ZoneRow = [
    zrow "Etc/GMT+12" "International Date Line West" (0 - 720) loc-dst-none (0 - 12),
    zrow "Pacific/Midway" "Midway" (0 - 660) loc-dst-none (0 - 11),
    zrow "Pacific/Honolulu" "Honolulu" (0 - 600) loc-dst-none (0 - 10),
    zrow "America/Anchorage" "Anchorage" (0 - 540) loc-dst-us (0 - 9),
    zrow "America/Los_Angeles" "Los Angeles" (0 - 480) loc-dst-us (0 - 8),
    zrow "America/Vancouver" "Vancouver" (0 - 480) loc-dst-us (0 - 8),
    zrow "America/Denver" "Denver" (0 - 420) loc-dst-us (0 - 7),
    zrow "America/Phoenix" "Phoenix" (0 - 420) loc-dst-none (0 - 7),
    zrow "America/Chicago" "Chicago" (0 - 360) loc-dst-us (0 - 6),
    zrow "America/Mexico_City" "Mexico City" (0 - 360) loc-dst-none (0 - 6),
    zrow "America/New_York" "New York" (0 - 300) loc-dst-us (0 - 5),
    zrow "America/Toronto" "Toronto" (0 - 300) loc-dst-us (0 - 5),
    zrow "America/Bogota" "Bogota" (0 - 300) loc-dst-none (0 - 5),
    zrow "America/Halifax" "Halifax" (0 - 240) loc-dst-us (0 - 4),
    zrow "America/Santiago" "Santiago" (0 - 240) loc-dst-south (0 - 4),
    zrow "America/St_Johns" "St John's" (0 - 210) loc-dst-us (0 - 4),
    zrow "America/Sao_Paulo" "Sao Paulo" (0 - 180) loc-dst-none (0 - 3),
    zrow "America/Argentina" "Buenos Aires" (0 - 180) loc-dst-none (0 - 3),
    zrow "Atlantic/South_Georgia" "South Georgia" (0 - 120) loc-dst-none (0 - 2),
    zrow "Atlantic/Azores" "Azores" (0 - 60) loc-dst-eu (0 - 1),
    zrow "Europe/London" "London" 0 loc-dst-eu 0,
    zrow "Europe/Lisbon" "Lisbon" 0 loc-dst-eu 0,
    zrow "UTC" "Coordinated Universal Time" 0 loc-dst-none 0,
    zrow "Africa/Lagos" "Lagos" 60 loc-dst-none 1,
    zrow "Europe/Paris" "Paris" 60 loc-dst-eu 1,
    zrow "Europe/Berlin" "Berlin" 60 loc-dst-eu 1,
